course: dictionary
lesson: 5463
title: One word, many meanings: lap
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Lap is a word with more than one meaning. Look at the words around it to find out which meaning the writer wants. «Picture the last lap on sports day: face red, chest heaving, heart thumping in your ears.» Here a lap is one time around the track, because it is sports day and people are running.
explain: «A seat is for a person, so put your bag on your lap or the floor when the bus is busy.» Your lap is the flat top part of your legs when you sit down. You can tell because a bag can sit on it, and a bag cannot sit on a track.
explain: Lap can also be a verb. A cat laps milk: it drinks by licking with its tongue. Waves lap at the shore: they move gently against the sand. To check, swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A lap is one time around a track, field or pool.
fact: Your lap is the flat top part of your legs when you sit down.
fact: To lap is to drink by licking with the tongue, like a cat.
fact: Water laps when it moves gently against something, like waves on a beach.
fact: To lap someone in a race is to get a whole lap ahead of them.
exercise: «The runners did three laps of the field.» How many times did they go around the field? | Three times around the field | Three times up a hill | Three hours in the sun | *Three times around the field, one lap at a time
exercise: «A cat sat on her lap while she read.» What is her lap? | A lap of the swimming pool | A cup for milk | *The flat top part of her legs when she sits down | The strap of her bag
exercise: Waves «lap» at the shore. What does lap mean here? | Race around the beach | Crash loudly into the rocks | Drink up the sea | *Move gently against the sand
test: «The winner lapped the slowest runner in the race.» What does lapped mean? | *Got a whole lap ahead of them | Was tired and sat down | Ate lunch quickly | Ran backwards
test: «Every morning, the dog laps water from his bowl.» What does laps mean here? | *Drinks by licking | Swims in a pool | Runs around a field | Sits on a chair
exam: In «Ella put her laptop on her lap, then ran three laps of the playground», what does lap mean in the second part? | The top of your legs | Waves on a beach | Drink by licking | *One time around a track, field or pool
